🚦 Transport Layer Protocol Simulation: UDP, TCP & SCTP
🎯 Objective
To design and simulate the behavior of User Datagram Protocol (UDP) , Transmission Control Protocol (TCP) , and Stream Control Transmission Protocol (SCTP) using Cisco Packet Tracer. The focus is on comparing connection establishment, reliability, and congestion control.

📊 Protocol Characteristics
Feature	UDP	TCP	SCTP
Connection	Connectionless	Connection-oriented	Association-oriented
Reliability	Unreliable (Best-effort)	Reliable (ACKs)	Reliable
Handshake	None	3-Way Handshake	4-Way Handshake
Data Flow	Byte-stream	Byte-stream	Message-oriented / Multi-streaming
Congestion Control	None	Yes	Yes
🖧 Network Topology
Devices: 3 Pairs of PC-to-PC / Server connections

Infrastructure:

1 Central Switch

1 Router (for inter-network traffic simulation)

Addressing: 192.168.1.0/24 subnet

🔍 Simulation Steps
1. 📤 UDP (User Datagram Protocol)
Observe the "fire and forget" nature.
➡️ No SYN / ACK packets are generated.

2. 🔗 TCP (Transmission Control Protocol)
Use Simulation Mode to capture the handshake sequence:
➡️ SYN → SYN-ACK → ACK

3. 📨 SCTP (Stream Control Transmission Protocol)
Analyze multi-streaming capabilities where multiple data streams are sent within a single association to prevent head-of-line blocking.
